WEBVTT

NOTE
The Dollet Communication Tower interior and satellite dish activation sequence.
Duration: approximately 1 minute 13 seconds.

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
The Communication Tower rises into the sky, its base barely visible. Inside, pipes, sliding floors, scaffolding, and green-lit machinery stretch upward.

00:07.000 --> 00:10.000
A large satellite dish looms as the ground shakes and a wrench falls from a toolbox through cracks.

00:10.000 --> 00:15.000
The wrench keeps falling, striking the structure as the ground fades far below.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
The stationary jet engines spool up, then surge into full power, spinning and blasting.

00:20.000 --> 00:22.000
Three switches flip upward

00:22.000 --> 00:30.000
The tower powers on and transforms into a massive communications fortress with glowing lights, antennae, and spinning dishes against the sunset sky.

00:30.000 --> 00:40.000
From the base of the tower, a capsule is catapulted into a central tube running up its core.

00:40.000 --> 00:43.000
Squall jolts as a capsule rushes past behind him through the tube.

00:43.000 --> 00:55.000
The capsule reaches its destination. Squall looks up in awe as the structure continues building and slowly rotates into position, angling above.

00:55.000 --> 01:02.000
The gigantic satellite dish fully deploys and opens, angled toward the sky against a glowing sunset horizon.

01:02.000 --> 01:06.000
The dish’s diamond core begins to glow, crackling with electricity.

01:06.000 --> 01:14.000
A towering satellite array rises above a calm ocean at sunset. Its top dish fires a blue beam into the clouds, while smaller dishes and green lights glow along its metal frame.
